.SH NAME
anpu-scan - Check a website for security problems


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu scan  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run ANPU's scan pipeline against a target URL.

.PP
ANPU only performs active network requests against targets you own or
are explicitly authorized to test.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--adversarial\fP[=false]
	enable adversarial hazardous probes (stateful multi-step, header/body/WS, JWT/mass-assign/race/smuggling/proto-pollute) — requires --confirm-authorized on authorized ultra targets only; Benign/LowImpact only, no data destruction

.PP
\fB--api-base-url\fP=""
	override the base URL detected from the OpenAPI schema (useful for scanning staging with a production schema)

.PP
\fB--auth-cookie\fP=[]
	cookie to include in every request, in name=value form (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--auth-header\fP=[]
	custom header to include in every request, in 'Name: Value' form (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--auth-role\fP=""
	label for the scan identity, e.g. admin, user (default: anonymous / user)

.PP
\fB--auth-token\fP=""
	bearer token to include in every request (Authorization: Bearer )

.PP
\fB--authz-cookie\fP=[]
	cookie for the second identity, in name=value form (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--authz-header\fP=[]
	custom header for the second identity, in 'Name: Value' form (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--authz-role\fP=""
	label for the second identity, e.g. user, anonymous (default: challenger)

.PP
\fB--authz-token\fP=""
	bearer token for the second (challenger) identity

.PP
\fB--auto-install\fP[=false]
	auto-install missing external tools mid-scan (go/pipx/docker; apt/choco best-effort) instead of skipping them

.PP
\fB--budget\fP=0s
	cap total scan wall time, e.g. 15m (queued stages stop between stages with per-phase coverage; 0 = uncapped)

.PP
\fB--checkpoint\fP=""
	write per-stage checkpoint snapshots here for --resume

.PP
\fB--confirm-authorized\fP[=false]
	confirm you are authorized to run hazardous adversarial probes against this target (required with --adversarial)

.PP
\fB--csv\fP[=false]
	write a CSV finding export (one row per finding)

.PP
\fB--delay\fP=0s
	fixed inter-request delay, e.g. 200ms or 1s (stacks with --rate-limit)

.PP
\fB--disable\fP=[]
	disable modules (comma-separated, e.g. --disable dirs,active) — simple alternative to many --no-* flags

.PP
\fB--enable\fP=[]
	enable modules (comma-separated, e.g. --enable portscan,naabu) — overrides profile defaults

.PP
\fB--fail-on\fP="none"
	return a non-zero exit status when findings meet/exceed this severity: none, low, medium, high, critical

.PP
\fB--ghost\fP[=false]
	low-visibility mode for contracted red-team engagements: Chrome 131 JA3, h2, GREASE, stable header set, Pareto 800-3500ms jitter, no anpu canary substring, proxy rotation, adaptive rate, payload polymorphism (combine with --proxy-pool and --adversarial for max power)

.PP
\fB--ghost-canary-prefix\fP=""
	custom ghost canary prefix (default "" when --ghost, no anpu substring; set to "anpu" to keep allowlist mode)

.PP
\fB--ghost-workers\fP=4
	parallel ghost workers for sharded active scanning (0 = sequential)

.PP
\fB--graphql\fP=""
	GraphQL endpoint URL to introspect (e.g. https://api.example.com/graphql)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for scan

.PP
\fB--html\fP[=true]
	write an HTML report

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	write a JSON report

.PP
\fB--jsonl\fP[=false]
	stream findings as JSON lines to stdout for piping (implies --silent human output)

.PP
\fB--junit\fP[=false]
	write a JUnit XML export for CI parsing

.PP
\fB-l\fP, \fB--list\fP=""
	read targets (one URL per line) from a file

.PP
\fB--md\fP[=false]
	write a Markdown finding summary

.PP
\fB--only\fP=[]
	run only this module(s) (e.g. --only dnsintel or --only headers,tls) — disables all others

.PP
\fB--openapi\fP=""
	path or URL to an OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.x schema; enables API-aware endpoint discovery and injection

.PP
\fB--output\fP="./reports"
	directory to write reports into

.PP
\fB--parallel\fP=8
	run snapshot-safe stages concurrently with N workers (1 = sequential, max 32)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP="safe"
	scan profile: safe, advanced, ultra (aliases: standard→advanced, deep→ultra)

.PP
\fB--proxy\fP=""
	route all HTTP traffic through a proxy (http/https/socks5), e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080 for Burp/ZAP; HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY/NO_PROXY env are honored when unset

.PP
\fB--proxy-pool\fP=""
	path to file with proxy URLs (one per line, http/https/socks5) for RoundRobin per-request rotation with healthcheck

.PP
\fB--rate-limit\fP=0
	max requests per second across all stages (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB--resume\fP=""
	resume an interrupted scan from a checkpoint file

.PP
\fB--risk-accept\fP=""
	suppress finding IDs listed in a YAML accept file (id/reason/expires)

.PP
\fB--sarif\fP[=false]
	write a SARIF report

.PP
\fB--scope-file\fP=""
	path to an allowlist file (one host per line); targets not listed abort before any request (hard stop)

.PP
\fB--silent\fP[=false]
	suppress banner, stage lines, and summary for clean piped output (reports still written)

.PP
\fB--stdin\fP[=false]
	read targets (one URL per line) from stdin, e.g. cat targets.txt | anpu scan --stdin

.PP
\fB--stealth\fP[=false]
	anonymous mode: random browser UA per request + jitter (combine with --proxy socks5://127.0.0.1:9050 for Tor anonymity)

.PP
\fB--unsafe\fP[=false]
	operator master override: implies adversarial+confirmed, lifts safe-purity filters, fuller wrapper strength (defaults/warnings/exclusions unchanged)

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	assume yes for install confirmations (scripts/CI)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


